; Stage 15 B6 — the tenth defect (`protocol-dyn-annot`), closed.
;
; Before B6 a `(dyn P)` in an ANNOTATION was never validated: `dyn-type` mints
; the box type from the spelling and the scope/existence question was asked only
; where a box was CONSTRUCTED, so this file compiled clean and emitted a
; `%__dyn.nope_Wholly-Absent` type for a protocol that does not exist anywhere.
;
; The placement was forced rather than chosen: `dyn-type` runs from a `defn`
; signature during `prescan-defn-signatures`, before any imported protocol is
; registered, so refusing there rejects every legal reference. B6 records the
; question instead — with the spelling, its line and the file's import
; environment — and `drain-dyn-annots` asks it after the whole graph is in
; (name-resolution.md §9.5).
;
; Nothing here constructs a box, which is the point: this is the annotation path
; and nothing else can reach it.
(defn takes-box ((box (dyn nope/Wholly-Absent))):i32 (return 0))

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
